# Keep the build context to what the image needs: pyproject.toml + uv.lock
# (dependencies are installed from the hash-pinned lock — the image must not
# drift from the tested dependency graph) + src/ (the project, built by the
# pinned hatchling backend) + docker/settings.toml (the shipped default
# settings). Everything below stays out of the context and the image layers.
#
# Local state and secret files are excluded explicitly (spec 32 ticket 16 /
# G22): the data dir, .env files, and the root-level providers / connectors /
# settings TOML files, which may hold feeder credentials, gate refs, or a
# fixed coop token. They are root-anchored so docker/settings.toml (shipped
# into the image on purpose) still matches.
.git
.venv
.uv
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
dist
*.egg-info
tests
specs
examples
docs
STATUS.md
data
.env*
/providers.toml
/connectors.toml
/settings.toml
